{"parentUuid":"7dda67f8-e513-4063-a16d-f344af5ffc74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcobxvHt7xSXjMJtbE2ue","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Autopsy complete and recorded. \n\n## Bottom line\nThe mid-May negative forward IC **is not a broken model** — it's mostly a measurement artifact. The **traded book** was down only −4.8%/−5.7% on its two worst entry dates, roughly flat on the rest of the mid-May window, then ripped **+9.7% → +24.5%** into June. The scary −0.06 IC came from three things the metric does badly:\n\n1. **Full-universe rank IC penalizes correct exclusions** — bottom-ranked junk (PSNL +47%, RGNX +55–99%) bounced in the selloff; the model rightly doesn't hold those, but the IC docks it anyway.\n2. **Overlapping windows** — 05-13→05-20 is ~one 20d episode counted as six.\n3. **A distressed name (AARD) floated to composite-rank #1** despite tier D + deep-drawdown flags, fell −45%, and polluted the gate — though it was never in the weighted book.\n\n## What I'd flag going forward\n- **The strategy behaved well mid-May** → early recovery, strong June. No action needed on the book.\n- **The gate itself is the weak link.** Now that it's un-frozen, it'll periodically fire on noise like this. Consider a follow-up to scope `forward_eval` IC to the **eligible/portfolio set** and de-overlap the rolling window, so it measures what you actually trade.\n\nEverything's captured in the memory note (PR #481, the fix, the autopsy conclusion). Want me to open a follow-up issue/PR to re-scope the gate, or leave that for you to decide after #481 merges?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":139248,"output_tokens":545,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"