{"parentUuid":"9d5e9d35-19f7-4fcf-b446-c1c36fe772f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcobzCsJssTykpfEUkCru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q3sgNiHhzXovVSe3fjRWPa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /mnt/c/Projects/biotech_screener/biotech-screener 2>/dev/null\ngh issue create \\\n  --title \"forward_eval gate: re-scope IC to tradeable set + de-overlap rolling window\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Context\n\nPR #481 fixed the *staleness* of the `forward_eval` gate (matured PIT forward returns were never backfilled, so the gate replayed a frozen `2026-04-03..04-20` window for months). With the caches backfilled, the gate now reads a real recent window (`2026-05-13..06-03`) at **mean_ic ≈ −0.06**.\n\nA forensic autopsy (2026-07-07) showed that negative reading is **largely a metric artifact, not model impairment** — the actual traded book was net-positive over the same entries. This issue tracks fixing the metric itself so it measures the model we trade and doesn't fire on noise.\n\n## Findings from the mid-May autopsy\n\n| Entry date | Weighted book fwd 20d |\n|---|---|\n| 2026-05-13 | −4.8% |\n| 2026-05-14 | −5.7% |\n| 05-15 → 05-20 | −0.4 to −1.0% |\n| 2026-05-21 | +9.7% |\n| 2026-05-27 | +12.2% |\n| 2026-05-29 | +13.7% |\n| 2026-06-03 | +24.5% |\n\nThe gate's IC disagreed sharply with this benign book performance because of three construction issues:\n\n1. **Full-universe rank IC penalizes correct exclusions.** The signal is `-actionable_rank`/`composite_rank` over *all ~295 names*. The biggest IC damage came from bottom-ranked names bouncing in the selloff — e.g. PSNL (rank ~281) +47%, RGNX (~220) +55–99% — names the model deliberately does not hold. Penalizing the model for not ranking junk highly is not informative about the strategy.\n\n2. **Overlapping forward windows are double-counted.** Snapshots 05-13→05-20 are 1–5 trading days apart, so their 20d-forward windows overlap ~90% — effectively one entry episode. The gate's flat mean over `lookback_n=10` treats them as independent, over-weighting a single bad episode.\n\n3. **Distressed names can float to the top of the full-universe ordering.** AARD was `composite_rank` #1 on 05-14 while tier D / headwind / `deep_drawdown`-flagged, and fell −45%. It was never in the weighted book (core bucket, unweighted) but was the single largest IC contributor — it pollutes the gate without touching the strategy.\n\n## Proposed changes (`tools/forward_eval_gate.py`)\n\n- **Scope the IC universe** to the tradeable/eligible set rather than the full universe — options to evaluate:\n  - portfolio names (`target_weight_pct > 0`), and/or\n  - `eligible == True`, and/or top-N by `actionable_rank`.\n  - Consider a weighted rank-IC or a decile spread (top vs bottom of the *eligible* set) alongside the plain Spearman.\n- **De-overlap the rolling window** — sample non-overlapping snapshot dates spaced ≥ `horizon` trading days apart, or down-weight overlapping dates, so one episode isn't counted `~horizon` times.\n- **Guard against distressed-name contamination** — sanity-check that names driving IC are actually in scope (e.g. exclude names the decision engine gates out), consistent with the scoping above.\n- Keep the gate **WARN-only / non-blocking**; this is about signal quality, not adding a hard gate.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Re-running the gate over `2026-05-13..06-03` on the tradeable set yields an IC consistent with the observed net-positive weighted-book performance (i.e. the mid-May window is no longer a strong false negative).\n- Overlapping-window inputs no longer produce `~horizon`-fold repetition of a single episode.\n- Existing tests (`tests/test_forward_eval_gate.py`) updated/extended for the new scoping.\n\n## References\n- PR #481 (staleness fix)\n- Autopsy scripts + weighted-book reconstruction (2026-07-07)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Open follow-up GitHub issue for gate re-scoping"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18,"cache_read_input_tokens":139962,"output_tokens":1633,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1633,"cache_read_input_tokens":139962,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcobzBXhDf59xUTympJRD","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb94e600-9ea9-4efd-a080-481ea4ae416a","timestamp":"2026-07-07T23:58:33.581Z","session_id":"61ba5fc3-05ad-4fb5-90d2-919f0eba7c7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/arrenchulz","sessionId":"61ba5fc3-05ad-4fb5-90d2-919f0eba7c7f","version":"2.1.203","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
