{"parentUuid":"524fc8e2-5eef-478b-a696-413847129e10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcpZKnNsX99Nfy8hWv2cY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cjht12D2cQUt1YZR7qcdTF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /mnt/c/Projects/biotech_screener/biotech-screener 2>/dev/null\nNEW=$(gh pr create --base main --head fix/forward-eval-pit-backfill-clean \\\n  --title \"fix(daily): backfill matured PIT forward returns by default\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Problem\n\nThe `forward_eval` gate discovers evaluable dates by scanning PIT price caches (`data/caches/price_pit/PIT/<date>/index.json`) for those whose 20d horizon is in `horizons_filled`. The daily run created the price **anchor** every day (`warm_price_pit=True`) but the **maturation backfill** (`warm_price_cache.py --backfill-all`) was opt-in (`--price-pit-backfill`, default off) and never passed by cron.\n\nResult: no cache past ~2026-04-20 ever had its h20 horizon filled, so the rolling-IC window was **frozen** at `2026-04-03..04-20` — byte-identical `mean_ic=-0.0064` on every run for months. The gate the model docs call the *live NO_MODEL_CHANGE forward-validation gate* was effectively blind to current data.\n\n## Fix\n\nMirror the existing `--no-warm-price-pit` opt-out pattern: the post-promotion backfill now runs **by default** in the daily pipeline; `--no-price-pit-backfill` opts out. Backfill is write-once and safe on reruns.\n\n- `price_pit_backfill` function default `False` -> `True`\n- CLI flag `--price-pit-backfill` -> `--no-price-pit-backfill`\n- caller wires `price_pit_backfill=not args.no_price_pit_backfill`\n\nSingle file: `tools/run_daily_production.py` (+6/-4).\n\n## Evidence\n\nAfter a manual `--backfill-all` (2026-07-07), h20 coverage advanced through `2026-06-03` and the gate window to `2026-05-13..06-03`. The refreshed IC read negative (mean -0.0597), but a forensic autopsy showed that is largely a **metric artifact** (full-universe rank IC penalizing correctly-excluded names that bounced; overlapping forward windows double-counted) — the actual weighted book was net-positive over those entries. Gate-quality follow-up tracked in #482.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No behavior change to the anchor step or gate logic; only whether the backfill runs.\n- Today's promoted `run_manifest` still shows the stale April value; it refreshes on the next daily run once caches are read.\n\nSupersedes #481 (which was accidentally opened from a contaminated base branch containing unrelated commits).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\")\necho \"NEW PR: $NEW\"\nNEWNUM=$(echo \"$NEW\" | grep -oE '[0-9]+$')\necho \"===== closing #481 with pointer =====\"\ngh pr close 481 --comment \"Superseded by #${NEWNUM}, which contains only the intended single-file change (\\`tools/run_daily_production.py\\`). This PR was accidentally opened from a contaminated base branch (\\`fix/sync-hermes-skills-dual-map-drop\\`) and carried two unrelated commits, causing merge conflicts and CI failures.\" --delete-branch 2>&1 | tail -4","description":"Open replacement PR and close #481"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":156006,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1250,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":156006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":174,"output_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":156006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":156006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CcpZKfaqjCxs8rPymim48","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d11abf1-b961-422