{"parentUuid":"5f879c86-0d63-4a46-9b84-b06dcbdb918b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Ccpb5amiRnEjhstXFyXet","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cra1QqgcyTYXvU8KQ1EYKf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/arrenchulz/.claude/projects/-home-arrenchulz/memory/project_forward_eval_gate_stale_2026_07_07.md","old_string":"**Why**: forward-eval health is a governance gate; a frozen ledger is worse than a failing one because it looks stable.","new_string":"**Deployed to shared/cron checkout 2026-07-08**: cron runs `tools/cron_daily_production.sh` → `python3 tools/run_daily_production.py` **from `/mnt/c/Projects/biotech_screener/biotech-screener/` itself** (this IS the shared checkout; it was 65 commits behind origin/main on branch `main`, 15 foreign dirty files). Did NOT pull 65 commits (blast radius). Instead applied the same 3-line diff directly to the live working-tree file → now byte-identical to origin/main's `run_daily_production.py` (that file hadn't drifted across the 65 commits except this change). Cron reads the working tree directly, so effective immediately (uncommitted working-tree edit, not a local commit — avoids a divergent local main). Verified: parses, `--no-price-pit-backfill` in `--help`, exit 0. ⚠️ Broader debt: the shared checkout is 65 commits behind main + main can't pass its own CI (mypy/lint/pytest-fixture) — separate cleanup needed.\n\n**Why**: forward-eval health is a governance gate; a frozen ledger is worse than a failing one because it looks stable."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":182955,"output_tokens":785,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1292,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inferen