{"parentUuid":"63010756-f68c-4b9d-811e-dc6541b40a24","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Ccq7rtmvzVPhPZqfdhMno","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SaK2e76dQaJWqveFKK28pB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /mnt/c/Projects/biotech_screener/biotech-screener 2>/dev/null\necho \"===== PR for #484 =====\"\ngh pr create --base main --head fix/cron-drift-guard-484 \\\n  --title \"fix(cron): warn when production checkout drifts behind origin/main\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nCloses #484 (drift-visibility portion).\n\nThe cron checkout does not auto-pull, so merged fixes silently do not run until it is fast-forwarded (bit the forward_eval fix, PRs #474/#475). Adds a non-blocking drift guard to `cron_daily_production.sh`: fetches origin/main (30s timeout, tolerates offline) and logs HEAD + commits-behind at run start — INFO if 1–5 behind, WARN past 5 flagging that stale code is running. Logs only; never aborts.\n\nDoes not fix the underlying auto-pull gap (a scheduled ff / dedicated prod clone is the durable fix) — this makes the drift visible so it can't silently persist.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2\n\necho \"===== PR for #482 =====\"\ngh pr create --base main --head fix/forward-eval-rescope-482 \\\n  --title \"fix(forward_eval): scope IC to tradeable set + de-overlap window\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nCloses #482.\n\nThe forward_eval gate computed a full-universe rank IC over the 10 most recent (near-adjacent) snapshots — a noisy proxy that (a) penalised the model for not ranking names it correctly excludes, and (b) double-counted one market episode ~10× via overlapping 20d-forward windows.\n\nChanges (`tools/forward_eval_gate.py`):\n- `scope=\"eligible\"` (new default): IC restricted to the tradeable set; also `portfolio`/`top_k`/`universe`. Falls back to universe (with a warning) if the scope column is absent, so a malformed rankings.csv can't silently blank the gate.\n- `min_gap_days` de-overlap in `_discover_pit_dates`; `evaluate_rolling_ic` defaults it to ≈ horizon trading days so retained windows don't overlap.\n- Records scope + min_gap_days in value/threshold.\n\nDefaults flow to the production caller with no GateConfig change. On the real 2026-05..06 caches this turns the spurious `-0.0597` WARN into a legitimate `+0.0332` PASS (de-overlap alone already flips the mean positive), matching the autopsy finding that the traded model was fine. WARN-only behaviour unchanged. 22/22 tests pass (new tests for scope + de-overlap).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2\n\necho \"===== DRAFT PR for #485 =====\"\ngh pr create --draft --base main --head fix/type-check-progress-485 \\\n  --title \"chore(mypy): incremental type-check pass (partial) — #485\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nPartial progress on #485 (green CI). **Draft** — `type-check` will still fail until the remaining ~30 mypy errors land.\n\nDone in this PR:\n- Disable `warn_unreachable` in the enforced-modules override — unsound while `strict_optional=false` (flags legitimate defensive None/regex/isinstance guards). Clears 23 false positives without touching runtime guards.\n- `milestone_optionality.py`: float / `List[Dict[str,Any]]` annotations (10 errors).\n- `rebalance_cost_model.py`: widen return to `dict[str, Any]` (2).\n- `review_queue.py`: annotate `groups` (1).\n\nNot yet done (~30 errors, ~18 files, catalogued in commit body): var-annotated sites, remaining int→float / dict widenings, `hash_utils` union-attr `type: ignore`s, and a **real latent bug** in `operator_delivery._is_duplicate` (calls `AlertDedupeStore()` with no `path` and non-existent `is_duplicate`/`record` — swallowed by a bare `except`, so dedup silently no-ops; needs a reviewed behavior fix, not just a type change).\n\nOut of scope (separate decisions): the `lint` job (repo-wide black/isort churn) and